---
description:
  Exercises the elk.box sub-algorithm, which positions nodes but does not route
  edges, so every edge here must fall back to a straight line between node
  centers. Guards against a regression where missing route data crashes on
  `points.filter`, and where the labelled edge's missing ELK label position
  renders as `translate(undefined, NaN)` instead of falling back correctly.
config:
  layout: elk.box
---
%% elk.box places nodes but does not route edges. Every edge here relies on the
%% straight-line fallback; without it the render throws on `points.filter`.
%% One edge is labelled: an unrouted edge has no ELK label position either, and
%% an unset one renders as `translate(undefined, NaN)`.
flowchart TD
  A[Start] -->|labelled| B[Middle]
  B --> C[End]
  A --> C
